se lists the same drug without specifying strength: this is a match!\n+   - Unit conversion is allowed (1 g = 1000 mg, 250 mcg = 0.25 mg).\n+\n+3. DOSAGE FORM (DIFFERENT FORM WITH SAME DRUG & STRENGTH -> \"review\"):\n+   - If the candidate is the EXACT SAME commercial drug with the SAME strength, but has a DIFFERENT dosage form (e.g. requested Cream vs warehouse has Ointment, or Drops vs Tablets):\n+     RETURN review with that candidate ID and explain in Arabic.\n+\n+4. PACKAGING, PACK SIZE & QUANTITY (DOES NOT PREVENT MATCH -> \"match\"):\n+   - Different tablet counts (15 vs 60 tablets, 20 vs 30 tablets), strip counts (2 strips vs 3 strips), packaging markers (باكت, كرتونة), and commercial price indicators (\"س ج\", \"سعر جديد\") DO NOT prevent a match. As long as brand and strength match, this is a match.\n+\n Return exactly one decision per case_id: match, no_match, or review. Return\n item_ids from that case's catalog only, and a short Arabic reason. no_match must\n have an empty item_ids array. match needs the IDs of the same product; review\n-may identify plausible candidates. Never invent a product or fill missing digits.\n-\n-Preserve brand identity, strength, concentration, dosage form and pack size.\n-Arabic/English transliteration, Arabic/Western digits, spacing, obvious missing\n-letters and reversed Arabic characters can be equivalent if identity is clear.\n-Exact unit conversion (1 g = 1000 mg) is allowed; changing the dose is not.\n-Different explicit strength, dosage form, route, release type or pack size is\n-not a match. A requested critical detail missing from the catalog is review,\n-not automatic agreement. A number without a clear unit must not be assigned a\n-made-up meaning. Do not infer strip size or assume a small pack means 15 g.\n-Do not use external knowledge to supply an unlisted strength or pack size.\n-If the request omits a detail and multiple catalog variants remain possible,\n-return review with those candidates rather than sele