ely on LLM alone.\n  2. **Terminal Error `Expecting value: line 1 column 1 (char 0)`**:\n     - Not an HTTP failure. Gemini returned Arabic conversational prose instead of JSON because system instructions were dropped.\n     - Pharmacy called `json.loads(text)` without validation/diagnostics.\n  3. **Runtime vs ZIP Discrepancy**:\n     - `orders.config.json` in the ZIP pointed to `openrouter/free`, while the terminal log pointed to Local API (`MSEMAX`).\n  4. **MSEMAX Does Not Select Model in AI Studio UI**:\n     - `DEFAULT_MODEL=gemini-3.8-flash` in `.env`, but `app.py` had zero automation to select the model in AI Studio's UI.\n     - Thinking Level HIGH was also unverified.\n  5. **Conversation Context Pollution**:\n     - `CLEAR_CHAT_ON_REQUEST=false` was feeding all batches into a single continuous conversation in AI Studio.\n  6. **Bug in `format_messages_to_prompt()`**:\n     - Condition `if system_lines and len(messages) <= 2:` caused system instructions to be dropped whenever message count > 2, leaving Gemini with no schema or rules, causing prose output!\n  7. **Strict JSON Contract & Diagnostics**:\n     - MSEMAX and Pharmacy must enforce a strict JSON contract with full raw response logging and error handling without unhandled exceptions.\n  8. **Execution Order**:\n     - The user explicitly instructed: **\"ابدأ بتوحيد الـbusiness rules والـruntime contract أولًا، ثم نصلح MSEMAX، وبعد ذلك فقط نقيس جودة Gemini على الحالات الحقيقية.\"** (Start by unifying business rules and runtime contract first, then fix MSEMAX, then evaluate Gemini on real cases).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Progress\n### Completed:\n1. **Business Rules Unification**:\n   - `D:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy\\review\\project_spec.md`: Updated Section 4 to reflect the new Decision Graph:\n     - Strength = red line (`NO_MATCH`).\n     - Dosage Form difference = `REVIEW`.\n     - Pack size & price markers = `MATCH`.\n     - AI restricted to OCR/identity, no generics/therapeutic alternatives.\n     - Deterministic Python guards.\n   - `D:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy\\review\\match_guards.py`:\n     - Separated `STRENGTH_KINDS = {\"mass_mg\", \"volume_ml\", \"percent\"}` from pack units (`tablets`, `capsules`, `strips`, `sachets`, `bare_numbers`).\n     - Rewrote `guard_decision`: explicit strength conflict -> `NO_MATCH`. Form conflict -> `REVIEW`. Pack size / count differences do NOT block `MATCH`. Reversal hints -> `REVIEW`.\n     - Validated syntax with `python -m py_compile`.\n   - `D:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy\\review\\probe_gemini_match.py`:\n     - Aligned `SYSTEM` prompt with the 4 critical rules.\n     - Aligned `CONTROLS` test cases (e.g. tablet count difference 15 vs 60 -> `match`; cream vs ointment with same strength -> `review`; missing strength in warehouse -> `match`).\n2. **Identification of Root Causes in `MSEMAX-GAIStudio\\app.py`**:\n   - Confirmed bug in line 599 of `app.py`: `if system_lines and len(messages) <= 2:` was dropping system prompt for any message array with >2 messages.\n   - Confirmed zero automation for model selection in `app.py`.\n   - Confirmed `CLEAR_CHAT_ON_REQUEST=false` in `.env`.\n\n### In Progress / Next Up:\n- Robust JSON contract and error handling in `D:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\src\\fast_match\\coordinator.py`.\n- Playwright automation and fixes in `D:\\AI_Engineer\\MSEMAX-GAIStudio\\app.py`.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Key Findings & Technical Decisions\n- **Why `Expecting value: line 1 column 1` happened**:\n  In `MSEMAX-GAIStudio\\app.py`, `format_messages_to_prompt()` received `[system, user]`, but if any extra turn or conversation state existed or message length exceeded 2, the system prompt was dropped completely. Gemini received only the raw JSON payload with no instructions to respond in JSON. Gemini responded in Arabic conversational prose. In `Pharmacy-agy\\src\\fast_match\\coordinator.py`, `re.search(r'\\{.*\\}')` failed to find JSON, leaving `clean` as the Arabic text. `json.loads(clean)` threw `JSONDecodeError: Expecting value: line 1 column 1 (char 0)`.\n- **Runtime Contract Requirement**:\n  Pharmacy's `_call_local_api()` must:\n  1. Never crash on non-JSON response.\n  2. Extract JSON from markdown blocks ```` ```json ```` or regex.\n  3. If unparseable, log raw response and diagnostics to `data/provider_errors.log` and return structured `provider_response_error` with `status: \"no_match\"` fallback.\n- **Model Selection in AI Studio**:\n  AI Studio UI has a model selector in the top toolbar or right panel. `app.py` must locate the model selector dropdown, check the current model text, and if it doesn't match the requested model (e.g. `gemini-3.8-flash`), click it, select the option, and verify.\n- **Thinking Mode Automation**:\n  `ensure_thinking_mode()` needs to verify the selected thinking level and log the actual value found.\n- **Conversation Isolation**:\n  Each batch must run in an isolated/clean session. In `MSEMAX-GAIStudio`, set `CLEAR_CHAT_ON_REQUEST=true` or use a fast \"New Chat\" click (`button[aria-label*=\"New prompt\"]` / `button[aria-label*=\"New chat\"]`) to avoid full page reloads while guaranteeing zero context bleeding.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Active Context\n- **Workspaces**:\n  - `D:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy` (Desktop app and fast matcher)\n  - `D:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy\\review` (Review scripts, spec, guards, and test controls)\n  - `D:\\AI_Engineer\\MSEMAX-GAIStudio` (FastAPI + Playwright gateway for Google AI Studio on port 8001)\n- **Python Environment**: `D:\\miniconda3\\envs\\venv\\python.exe`\n- **Port**: 8001 (Google AI Studio Gateway)\n\n---\n\n## 5. Next Steps (In Priority Order)\n\n### Step 1: Update Pharmacy-agy (`src/fast_match/coordinator.py`)\n1. **Update `_call_local_api()`**:\n   - Implement robust JSON extraction (handling markdown fences ```` ```json ````, `{...}`, and `[...]`).\n   - If non-JSON text is returned:\n     - Do NOT raise unhandled `RuntimeError`/`json.JSONDecodeError`.\n     - Write timestamp, prompt snippet, response status, and full raw content to `data/provider_errors.log`.\n     - Return clean fallback decisions or retry safely.\n2. **Synchronize SYSTEM_PROMPT & guards in `coordinator.py`**:\n   - Ensure `SYSTEM_PROMPT` in `coordinator.py` strictly aligns with the 4 approved rules.\n\n### Step 2: Fix `MSEMAX-GAIStudio\\app.py`\n1. **Fix `format_messages_to_prompt()`**:\n   - Remove the `len(messages) <= 2` restriction.\n   - ALWAYS prepend system instructions:\n     ```python\n     if system_lines:\n         return f\"[System Instructions]\\n\" + \"\\n\".join(system_lines) + \"\\n\\n\" + (last_user or dialogue)\n     ```\n2. **Add `ensure_model(model_name)` in `WebHookBrowserManager`**:\n   - Inspect model selector in AI Studio UI (`mat-select[aria-label*=\"Model\"]`, `.model-selector`, etc.).\n   - Click and select `model_name` if not already active.\n   - Log the verified model.\n3. **Verify and harden `ensure_thinking_mode()`**:\n   - Verify that Thinking Level is actually set and log the confirmed level.\n4. **Context Isolation**:\n   - In `.env` and `app.py`, default `CLEAR_CHAT_ON_REQUEST=true`.\n   - Ensure clean session reset per batch without full page reload if possible (click \"New chat\" button in UI).\n5. **Add Comprehensive Request Logging**:\n   - Log: actual UI model, actual thinking level, conversation isolation flag, prompt chars, response chars, raw response snippet, whether response is valid JSON.\n\n### Step 3: Verification & Real Case Testing\n1. Test with small synthetic batches and verify `data/provider_errors.log` stays empty and JSON is returned reliably.\n2. Run `probe_gemini_match.py` and verify all 10 controls pass with the new Decision Graph.\n3. Test a batch through `fast_main.py` / `desktop_app` against MSEMAX-GAIStudio.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Commitments & Constraints\n- Follow the user's explicit sequence: **Unify business rules & runtime contract first -> Fix MSEMAX -> Evaluate real cases.**\n- Never let `json.loads` crash without diagnostics when LLM returns non-JSON text.\n- Preserve the 4 core business rules across all files.\n</summary>\n\nYou have the 244 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: agent]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.agents/agents/desktop-builder/agent.md\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T22:17:02Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: agent]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.agents/agents/pharmacy-builder/agent.md\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T10:46:04Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1790101953275]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.tempmediaStorage/media_1790101953275.png\nLast Edited: 2026-09-22T18:32:33Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1790006220414]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.user_uploaded/media_1790006220414.png\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T15:57:26Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1790006245677]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.user_uploaded/media_1790006245677.png\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T15:57:26Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1790008142552]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.user_uploaded/media_1790008142552.png\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T16:29:03Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1790030764891]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.user_uploaded/media_1790030764891.png\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T22:46:21Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1790030964763]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.user_uploaded/media_1790030964763.png\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T22:49:25Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1790031115353]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.user_uploaded/media_1790031115353.png\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T22:53:02Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1790032058386]\nPath: file:/